      "message": "Since `url` (line 80) and `trace` (line 83) prepend a newline (`\\nEndpoint:` and `\\nTrace Id:`), appending two newlines here (`\\n\\n`) means that when `tip` and `url` are both present, `err` will contain `\\n\\n\\nEndpoint:`. In HTML elements with `white-space: pre-wrap` (such as `gr-error-dialog`), 3 consecutive newlines render as TWO blank lines between the tip and the endpoint line.\n\nConsider changing this to `\\n${tip}\\n` so there is exactly 1 blank line (`\\n\\n`) between the tip and the endpoint/trace info.",
